{"id":"vol9-08","section":4,"path":"bank/listening/vol9-08/audio-4.m4a","model":"small","duration":419.4,"segments":[{"start":0.0,"end":3.18,"text":"Now turn to section 4 on page 7.","words":[["Now",0.0,0.28],["turn",0.28,0.58],["to",0.58,0.78],["section",0.78,1.04],["4",1.04,1.66],["on",1.66,2.4],["page",2.4,2.7],["7.",2.7,3.18]]},{"start":5.46,"end":10.38,"text":"Section 4. You will hear part of a lecture on rural development.","words":[["Section",5.46,5.68],["4.",5.68,6.2],["You",7.18,7.44],["will",7.44,7.64],["hear",7.64,7.88],["part",7.88,8.22],["of",8.22,8.38],["a",8.38,8.54],["lecture",8.54,8.8],["on",8.8,9.28],["rural",9.28,9.72],["development.",9.72,10.38]]},{"start":11.4,"end":16.7,"text":"First you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40 on page 7.","words":[["First",11.4,12.02],["you",12.02,12.26],["have",12.26,12.4],["some",12.4,12.58],["time",12.58,12.96],["to",12.96,13.24],["look",13.24,13.4],["at",13.4,13.54],["questions",13.54,13.84],["31",13.84,14.64],["to",14.64,14.88],["40",14.88,15.3],["on",15.3,15.9],["page",15.9,16.22],["7.",16.22,16.7]]},{"start":57.15,"end":60.83,"text":"Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.","words":[["Now",57.15,57.49],["listen",57.49,57.83],["carefully",57.83,58.31],["and",58.31,58.65],["answer",58.65,59.03],["questions",59.03,59.41],["31",59.41,60.27],["to",60.27,60.47],["40.",60.47,60.83]]},{"start":64.49,"end":69.43,"text":"Good morning everyone. Now you'll remember that last week we looked at the migration of people","words":[["Good",64.49,64.97],["morning",64.97,65.21],["everyone.",65.21,65.59],["Now",66.47,66.73],["you'll",66.73,66.95],["remember",66.95,67.13],["that",67.13,67.35],["last",67.35,67.57],["week",67.57,67.81],["we",67.81,67.99],["looked",67.99,68.17],["at",68.17,68.33],["the",68.33,68.43],["migration",68.43,68.75],["of",68.75,69.13],["people",69.13,69.43]]},{"start":69.43,"end":75.43,"text":"from the interior of West Africa to various coastal towns with special reference to Ghana.","words":[["from",69.43,69.71],["the",69.71,69.87],["interior",69.87,70.39],["of",70.39,70.81],["West",70.81,71.07],["Africa",71.07,71.41],["to",71.41,72.07],["various",72.07,72.47],["coastal",72.47,72.89],["towns",72.89,73.43],["with",73.43,74.11],["special",74.11,74.49],["reference",74.49,74.93],["to",74.93,75.15],["Ghana.",75.15,75.43]]},{"start":76.69,"end":81.33,"text":"Today we're going to focus on the people known as the Burbers who live in North Africa.","words":[["Today",76.69,77.11],["we're",77.11,77.43],["going",77.43,77.55],["to",77.55,77.67],["focus",77.67,77.95],["on",77.95,78.19],["the",78.19,78.29],["people",78.29,78.47],["known",78.47,78.75],["as",78.75,78.97],["the",78.97,79.21],["Burbers",79.21,79.75],["who",79.75,80.35],["live",80.35,80.51],["in",80.51,80.65],["North",80.65,80.91],["Africa.",80.91,81.33]]},{"start":82.39,"end":87.91,"text":"The Burbers inhabited this part of Africa as long ago as the 7th century and their society","words":[["The",82.39,82.57],["Burbers",82.57,82.87],["inhabited",82.87,83.37],["this",83.37,83.61],["part",83.61,83.85],["of",83.85,83.99],["Africa",83.99,84.33],["as",84.33,84.81],["long",84.81,84.99],["ago",84.99,85.27],["as",85.27,85.53],["the",85.53,85.73],["7th",85.73,86.61],["century",86.61,86.61],["and",86.61,87.35],["their",87.35,87.49],["society",87.49,87.91]]},{"start":87.91,"end":93.63,"text":"was based on tribes which were scattered throughout a number of countries, Algeria, Morocco,","words":[["was",87.91,88.23],["based",88.23,88.51],["on",88.51,88.77],["tribes",88.77,89.35],["which",89.35,89.93],["were",89.93,90.07],["scattered",90.07,90.37],["throughout",90.37,90.73],["a",90.73,90.95],["number",90.95,91.19],["of",91.19,91.39],["countries,",91.39,91.83],["Algeria,",92.53,93.23],["Morocco,",93.39,93.63]]},{"start":94.25,"end":95.47,"text":"Libya and Mali.","words":[["Libya",94.25,94.51],["and",94.51,95.05],["Mali.",95.05,95.47]]},{"start":95.47,"end":101.89,"text":"century. However, at some point in the 12th century, the area was invaded by Bedouin Arabs.","words":[["century.",95.47,95.57],["However,",96.27,96.79],["at",97.43,97.77],["some",97.77,97.99],["point",97.99,98.27],["in",98.27,98.51],["the",98.51,98.61],["12th",98.61,99.39],["century,",99.39,99.39],["the",99.67,99.77],["area",99.77,100.05],["was",100.05,100.25],["invaded",100.25,100.63],["by",100.63,100.91],["Bedouin",100.91,101.45],["Arabs.",101.45,101.89]]},{"start":102.79,"end":107.97,"text":"These people destroyed the Berbers' peasant economy. As a result, many Berbers left their","words":[["These",102.79,103.01],["people",103.01,103.27],["destroyed",103.27,103.63],["the",103.63,103.81],["Berbers'",103.81,104.09],["peasant",104.21,104.45],["economy.",104.45,104.89],["As",106.01,106.21],["a",106.21,106.29],["result,",106.29,106.59],["many",106.87,107.05],["Berbers",107.05,107.43],["left",107.43,107.71],["their",107.71,107.97]]},{"start":107.97,"end":113.03,"text":"settlements to lead a nomadic life by wandering with their animals through the deserts and","words":[["settlements",107.97,108.33],["to",108.33,108.69],["lead",108.69,108.87],["a",108.87,109.09],["nomadic",109.09,109.45],["life",109.45,109.97],["by",109.97,110.73],["wandering",110.73,111.05],["with",111.05,111.35],["their",111.35,111.47],["animals",111.47,111.89],["through",111.89,112.25],["the",112.25,112.39],["deserts",112.39,112.91],["and",112.91,113.03]]},{"start":113.03,"end":118.49,"text":"across the different mountains. Over the centuries, many Berbers migrated to other","words":[["across",113.03,113.27],["the",113.27,113.55],["different",113.55,113.79],["mountains.",113.79,114.21],["Over",115.47,115.85],["the",115.85,115.97],["centuries,",115.97,116.41],["many",116.87,117.19],["Berbers",117.19,117.55],["migrated",117.55,117.85],["to",117.85,118.29],["other",118.29,118.49]]},{"start":118.49,"end":124.05,"text":"countries like Spain and France to work as laborers, taking with them their culture","words":[["countries",118.49,118.91],["like",118.91,119.27],["Spain",119.27,119.67],["and",119.67,119.87],["France",119.87,120.33],["to",120.33,121.07],["work",121.07,121.27],["as",121.27,121.45],["laborers,",121.45,122.07],["taking",122.53,122.91],["with",122.91,123.15],["them",123.15,123.47],["their",123.47,123.69],["culture",123.69,124.05]]},{"start":124.05,"end":129.89,"text":"and traditions and their descendants remain there until this day. Not all the","words":[["and",124.05,124.35],["traditions",124.35,124.67],["and",124.67,125.55],["their",125.55,125.69],["descendants",125.69,126.03],["remain",126.03,126.43],["there",126.43,126.77],["until",126.77,127.23],["this",127.23,127.49],["day.",127.49,127.73],["Not",128.79,129.29],["all",129.29,129.73],["the",129.73,129.89]]},{"start":129.89,"end":135.25,"text":"burbers led a fully nomadic life. There were three different groups. Some became","words":[["burbers",129.89,130.17],["led",130.17,130.41],["a",130.41,130.55],["fully",130.55,130.73],["nomadic",130.73,131.19],["life.",131.19,131.57],["There",132.09,132.27],["were",132.27,132.37],["three",132.37,132.67],["different",132.67,133.15],["groups.",133.15,133.69],["Some",134.51,134.87],["became",134.87,135.25]]},{"start":135.25,"end":139.51,"text":"farmers cultivating the lowlands in the winter and grazing their flocks of","words":[["farmers",135.25,135.77],["cultivating",135.77,136.61],["the",136.61,136.79],["lowlands",136.79,137.17],["in",137.17,137.41],["the",137.41,137.51],["winter",137.51,137.73],["and",137.73,138.55],["grazing",138.55,138.87],["their",138.87,139.09],["flocks",139.09,139.41],["of",139.41,139.51]]},{"start":139.51,"end":144.23,"text":"animals in the mountains during the summer. They are called seasonal nomads.","words":[["animals",139.51,139.85],["in",139.85,140.13],["the",140.13,140.21],["mountains",140.21,140.47],["during",140.47,140.85],["the",140.85,141.03],["summer.",141.03,141.29],["They",142.13,142.37],["are",142.37,142.53],["called",142.53,142.83],["seasonal",142.83,143.57],["nomads.",143.57,144.23]]},{"start":145.11,"end":149.49,"text":"Some burbers who led a completely nomadic life tended to move from one","words":[["Some",145.11,145.43],["burbers",145.43,145.77],["who",145.77,145.99],["led",145.99,146.17],["a",146.17,146.27],["completely",146.27,146.67],["nomadic",146.67,147.29],["life",147.29,147.83],["tended",147.83,148.49],["to",148.49,148.75],["move",148.75,148.95],["from",148.95,149.19],["one",149.19,149.49]]},{"start":149.49,"end":156.03,"text":"oasis to another. A third group settled by the oases and grew fruit and vegetables","words":[["oasis",149.49,150.05],["to",150.05,150.49],["another.",150.49,150.81],["A",152.05,152.25],["third",152.25,152.59],["group",152.59,152.91],["settled",152.91,153.51],["by",153.51,153.81],["the",153.81,153.97],["oases",153.97,154.37],["and",154.37,154.95],["grew",154.95,155.17],["fruit",155.17,155.45],["and",155.45,155.61],["vegetables",155.61,156.03]]},{"start":156.03,"end":160.99,"text":"like dates and eggplants as well as making olive oil which they used for","words":[["like",156.03,156.45],["dates",156.45,157.01],["and",157.01,157.35],["eggplants",157.35,157.91],["as",157.91,158.73],["well",158.73,158.87],["as",158.87,158.97],["making",158.97,159.21],["olive",159.21,159.49],["oil",159.49,159.83],["which",159.83,160.35],["they",160.35,160.57],["used",160.57,160.83],["for",160.83,160.99]]},{"start":160.99,"end":167.05,"text":"cooking. Traditionally burburs kept cattle sheep and goats together with oxen","words":[["cooking.",160.99,161.21],["Traditionally",162.45,163.09],["burburs",163.09,163.87],["kept",163.87,164.07],["cattle",164.07,164.45],["sheep",164.45,164.73],["and",164.73,164.93],["goats",164.93,165.33],["together",165.33,166.11],["with",166.11,166.43],["oxen",166.43,167.05]]},{"start":167.05,"end":172.75,"text":"mules and horses. Now in the Sahel region of North Africa that's the area","words":[["mules",167.05,167.39],["and",167.39,167.59],["horses.",167.59,167.89],["Now",169.33,169.49],["in",169.49,169.63],["the",169.63,169.73],["Sahel",169.73,170.17],["region",170.17,170.53],["of",170.53,170.73],["North",170.73,170.91],["Africa",170.91,171.27],["that's",171.27,172.39],["the",172.39,172.51],["area",172.51,172.75]]},{"start":172.75,"end":176.73,"text":"south of the Sahara Desert the region became and still is becoming","words":[["south",172.75,173.13],["of",173.13,173.33],["the",173.33,173.45],["Sahara",173.45,173.79],["Desert",173.79,174.11],["the",174.11,174.91],["region",174.91,175.19],["became",175.19,175.59],["and",175.59,175.97],["still",175.97,176.23],["is",176.23,176.41],["becoming",176.41,176.73]]},{"start":176.73,"end":182.37,"text":"becoming increasingly dry and arid. So the Berbers relied more and more on camels for","words":[["becoming",176.73,176.85],["increasingly",176.85,177.53],["dry",177.53,177.91],["and",177.91,178.25],["arid.",178.25,178.69],["So",179.15,179.55],["the",179.55,179.73],["Berbers",179.73,179.99],["relied",179.99,180.35],["more",180.35,180.71],["and",180.71,180.87],["more",180.87,181.13],["on",181.13,181.63],["camels",181.63,182.19],["for",182.19,182.37]]},{"start":182.37,"end":188.89,"text":"transporting their families and their goods. How did these different groups of people survive","words":[["transporting",182.37,182.87],["their",182.87,183.13],["families",183.13,183.51],["and",183.51,184.11],["their",184.11,184.27],["goods.",184.27,184.53],["How",186.81,187.01],["did",187.01,187.17],["these",187.17,187.37],["different",187.37,187.71],["groups",187.71,187.99],["of",187.99,188.15],["people",188.15,188.41],["survive",188.41,188.89]]},{"start":188.89,"end":196.21,"text":"in such harsh conditions? Where did they live? Well, Berbers who stayed put in one place","words":[["in",188.89,189.17],["such",189.17,189.41],["harsh",189.41,189.93],["conditions?",189.93,190.53],["Where",191.47,191.75],["did",191.75,191.89],["they",191.89,192.01],["live?",192.01,192.27],["Well,",193.23,193.53],["Berbers",194.25,194.57],["who",194.57,194.79],["stayed",194.79,195.07],["put",195.07,195.29],["in",195.29,195.57],["one",195.57,195.75],["place",195.75,196.21]]},{"start":196.21,"end":203.41,"text":"built single-story stone houses for protection by quarrying the local rock. Whereas nomadic","words":[["built",196.21,196.71],["single",196.71,197.09],["-story",197.09,197.45],["stone",197.45,197.81],["houses",197.81,198.23],["for",198.23,198.85],["protection",198.85,199.31],["by",199.31,199.99],["quarrying",199.99,200.43],["the",200.43,200.63],["local",200.63,200.91],["rock.",200.91,201.35],["Whereas",202.15,202.71],["nomadic",202.71,203.41]]},{"start":203.41,"end":209.01,"text":"Burbers carried their homes with them and erected temporary tents. Settled Burbers developed","words":[["Burbers",203.41,203.85],["carried",203.85,204.17],["their",204.17,204.47],["homes",204.47,204.77],["with",204.77,205.07],["them",205.07,205.31],["and",205.31,205.83],["erected",205.83,206.33],["temporary",206.33,206.69],["tents.",206.69,207.15],["Settled",207.77,208.17],["Burbers",208.17,208.53],["developed",208.53,209.01]]},{"start":209.01,"end":215.11,"text":"various small-scale industries such as pottery making and weaving, but these tasks were generally","words":[["various",209.01,209.41],["small",209.41,209.79],["-scale",209.79,210.03],["industries",210.03,210.63],["such",210.63,211.35],["as",211.35,211.57],["pottery",211.57,212.07],["making",212.07,212.41],["and",212.41,212.77],["weaving,",212.77,213.09],["but",213.51,214.07],["these",214.07,214.25],["tasks",214.25,214.59],["were",214.59,214.83],["generally",214.83,215.11]]},{"start":215.11,"end":221.39,"text":"left to the Burber women. As you might expect though, the life of a settled community was","words":[["left",215.11,215.49],["to",215.49,215.71],["the",215.71,215.87],["Burber",215.87,216.13],["women.",216.13,216.37],["As",217.61,217.89],["you",217.89,218.03],["might",218.03,218.23],["expect",218.23,218.51],["though,",218.51,218.91],["the",219.35,219.45],["life",219.45,219.73],["of",219.73,219.89],["a",219.89,220.01],["settled",220.01,220.27],["community",220.27,220.85],["was",220.85,221.39]]},{"start":221.39,"end":226.49,"text":"governed by the men who met regularly in the village square to discuss affairs and make decisions.","words":[["governed",221.39,221.63],["by",221.63,221.87],["the",221.87,222.03],["men",222.03,222.21],["who",222.21,222.95],["met",222.95,223.13],["regularly",223.13,223.61],["in",223.61,224.03],["the",224.03,224.15],["village",224.15,224.37],["square",224.37,224.73],["to",224.73,225.03],["discuss",225.03,225.35],["affairs",225.35,225.73],["and",225.73,225.95],["make",225.95,226.11],["decisions.",226.11,226.49]]},{"start":231.82,"end":237.48,"text":"Now let's turn to the Tuaregs who belong to a nomadic Burber group and move mainly in the","words":[["Now",231.82,232.12],["let's",232.12,232.36],["turn",232.36,232.56],["to",232.56,232.76],["the",232.76,232.88],["Tuaregs",232.88,233.66],["who",233.66,234.06],["belong",234.06,234.36],["to",234.36,234.6],["a",234.6,234.68],["nomadic",234.68,235.08],["Burber",235.08,235.52],["group",235.52,235.84],["and",235.84,236.5],["move",236.5,236.7],["mainly",236.7,237.04],["in",237.04,237.4],["the",237.4,237.48]]},{"start":237.48,"end":244.46,"text":"central and western Sahara Desert north of the River Niger. The word Tuareg comes from","words":[["central",237.48,237.88],["and",237.88,238.18],["western",238.18,238.48],["Sahara",238.48,238.98],["Desert",238.98,239.3],["north",239.3,240.1],["of",240.1,240.52],["the",240.52,240.64],["River",240.64,240.76],["Niger.",240.76,241.14],["The",242.18,242.52],["word",242.52,242.84],["Tuareg",242.84,243.7],["comes",243.7,244.22],["from",244.22,244.46]]},{"start":244.46,"end":251.98,"text":"the Arabic Tawaric and means God-Forsaken. Desert Tuareg carried tents made of strips","words":[["the",244.46,244.58],["Arabic",244.58,244.96],["Tawaric",244.96,246.02],["and",246.02,246.74],["means",246.74,247.02],["God",247.02,247.6],["-Forsaken.",247.6,248.18],["Desert",249.3,249.94],["Tuareg",249.94,250.58],["carried",250.58,250.88],["tents",250.88,251.26],["made",251.26,251.62],["of",251.62,251.76],["strips",251.76,251.98]]},{"start":251.98,"end":257.7,"text":"of goat skins sewn together. As many as 40 skins were needed to make a complete tent.","words":[["of",251.98,252.24],["goat",252.24,252.44],["skins",252.44,252.82],["sewn",252.82,253.14],["together.",253.14,253.54],["As",254.44,254.72],["many",254.72,254.96],["as",254.96,255.24],["40",255.24,255.76],["skins",255.76,256.16],["were",256.16,256.34],["needed",256.34,256.52],["to",256.52,256.72],["make",256.72,256.88],["a",256.88,256.98],["complete",256.98,257.26],["tent.",257.26,257.7]]},{"start":258.64,"end":263.92,"text":"If the skins weren't available, they wove mats made of grass or palm leaves and hung","words":[["If",258.64,258.96],["the",258.96,259.18],["skins",259.18,259.4],["weren't",259.4,259.74],["available,",259.74,260.2],["they",260.48,260.84],["wove",260.84,261.1],["mats",261.1,261.46],["made",261.46,261.74],["of",261.74,261.9],["grass",261.9,262.18],["or",262.18,262.48],["palm",262.48,262.78],["leaves",262.78,263.08],["and",263.08,263.72],["hung",263.72,263.92]]},{"start":263.92,"end":271.12,"text":"them over a frame so that the tent looked like a humped dome. Tuareg society was traditionally","words":[["them",263.92,264.06],["over",264.06,264.38],["a",264.38,264.58],["frame",264.58,264.92],["so",264.92,265.58],["that",265.58,265.72],["the",265.72,265.88],["tent",265.88,266.04],["looked",266.04,266.28],["like",266.28,266.58],["a",266.58,266.68],["humped",266.68,267.16],["dome.",267.16,267.62],["Tuareg",268.88,269.52],["society",269.52,269.82],["was",269.82,270.5],["traditionally",270.5,271.12]]},{"start":271.12,"end":278.28,"text":"very feudal and organized as a strict hierarchy ranging from nobles or aristocrats downwards","words":[["very",271.12,271.5],["feudal",271.5,272.16],["and",272.16,272.76],["organized",272.76,273.22],["as",273.22,273.6],["a",273.6,273.74],["strict",273.74,273.96],["hierarchy",273.96,274.6],["ranging",274.6,275.48],["from",275.48,275.78],["nobles",275.78,276.34],["or",276.34,276.66],["aristocrats",276.66,277.5],["downwards",277.5,278.28]]},{"start":278.28,"end":285.96,"text":"to laborers whose ancestors had once been slaves. Tuaregs were famous for their warlike qualities","words":[["to",278.28,278.6],["laborers",278.6,279.26],["whose",279.26,279.86],["ancestors",279.86,280.42],["had",280.42,280.76],["once",280.76,281.0],["been",281.0,281.22],["slaves.",281.22,281.72],["Tuaregs",283.22,283.94],["were",283.94,284.22],["famous",284.22,284.54],["for",284.54,284.82],["their",284.82,284.98],["warlike",284.98,285.4],["qualities",285.4,285.96]]},{"start":285.96,"end":292.92,"text":"and fierce independence. In fact, one of the greatest insults was to suggest to a Tuareg","words":[["and",285.96,286.56],["fierce",286.56,286.96],["independence.",286.96,287.72],["In",288.62,288.8],["fact,",288.8,289.12],["one",289.64,289.8],["of",289.8,289.92],["the",289.92,290.04],["greatest",290.04,290.28],["insults",290.28,291.14],["was",291.14,291.36],["to",291.36,291.56],["suggest",291.56,291.96],["to",291.96,292.2],["a",292.2,292.3],["Tuareg",292.3,292.92]]},{"start":292.92,"end":298.9,"text":"his father had died in his bed and not while fighting. Tuareg men were","words":[["his",292.92,293.42],["father",293.42,293.8],["had",293.8,294.04],["died",294.04,294.26],["in",294.26,294.44],["his",294.44,294.56],["bed",294.56,294.84],["and",294.84,295.52],["not",295.52,295.72],["while",295.72,296.08],["fighting.",296.08,296.5],["Tuareg",297.84,298.4],["men",298.4,298.62],["were",298.62,298.9]]},{"start":298.9,"end":303.5,"text":"sometimes called blue men as all adult males were a dark blue veil in the","words":[["sometimes",298.9,299.3],["called",299.3,299.7],["blue",299.7,299.98],["men",299.98,300.32],["as",300.32,301.12],["all",301.12,301.28],["adult",301.28,301.6],["males",301.6,301.88],["were",301.88,302.18],["a",302.18,302.34],["dark",302.34,302.56],["blue",302.56,302.82],["veil",302.82,303.1],["in",303.1,303.42],["the",303.42,303.5]]},{"start":303.5,"end":308.62,"text":"presence of women, strangers and in-laws. Legend had it that a Tuareg man","words":[["presence",303.5,303.76],["of",303.76,304.0],["women,",304.0,304.24],["strangers",304.84,305.12],["and",305.12,305.56],["in",305.56,305.78],["-laws.",305.78,305.94],["Legend",306.7,307.06],["had",307.06,307.34],["it",307.34,307.5],["that",307.5,307.68],["a",307.68,307.8],["Tuareg",307.8,308.34],["man",308.34,308.62]]},{"start":308.62,"end":313.8,"text":"couldn't be recognized unless he was wearing this veil. But this custom of","words":[["couldn't",308.62,309.26],["be",309.26,309.38],["recognized",309.38,309.92],["unless",309.92,310.56],["he",310.56,310.78],["was",310.78,310.88],["wearing",310.88,311.16],["this",311.16,311.5],["veil.",311.5,312.0],["But",312.8,313.1],["this",313.1,313.28],["custom",313.28,313.62],["of",313.62,313.8]]},{"start":313.8,"end":318.44,"text":"the veil began to disappear as more and more Tuaregs became urbanized and moved","words":[["the",313.8,313.9],["veil",313.9,314.1],["began",314.1,314.46],["to",314.46,314.64],["disappear",314.64,315.0],["as",315.0,315.82],["more",315.82,316.1],["and",316.1,316.24],["more",316.24,316.38],["Tuaregs",316.38,316.96],["became",316.96,317.26],["urbanized",317.26,318.06],["and",318.06,318.22],["moved",318.22,318.44]]},{"start":318.44,"end":324.9,"text":"to the towns. I mentioned earlier how dry the Sahel region has become and there","words":[["to",318.44,318.6],["the",318.6,318.7],["towns.",318.7,319.14],["I",320.26,320.86],["mentioned",320.86,321.22],["earlier",321.22,321.68],["how",321.68,322.14],["dry",322.14,322.48],["the",322.48,322.68],["Sahel",322.68,323.04],["region",323.04,323.42],["has",323.42,323.7],["become",323.7,324.02],["and",324.02,324.78],["there",324.78,324.9]]},{"start":324.9,"end":329.42,"text":"have been very severe droughts over the past 30 years. This has meant that the","words":[["have",324.9,324.98],["been",324.98,325.14],["very",325.14,325.38],["severe",325.38,325.66],["droughts",325.66,326.26],["over",326.26,326.38],["the",326.38,326.48],["past",326.48,326.74],["30",326.74,327.08],["years.",327.08,327.48],["This",328.46,328.68],["has",328.68,328.8],["meant",328.8,329.02],["that",329.02,329.28],["the",329.28,329.42]]},{"start":329.42,"end":334.24,"text":"number of Tuaregs living in the area has declined. Those whose animals were","words":[["number",329.42,329.76],["of",329.76,329.96],["Tuaregs",329.96,330.48],["living",330.48,330.74],["in",330.74,330.96],["the",330.96,331.06],["area",331.06,331.34],["has",331.34,331.62],["declined.",331.62,332.02],["Those",333.18,333.38],["whose",333.38,333.64],["animals",333.64,334.0],["were",334.0,334.24]]},{"start":334.24,"end":338.18,"text":"fortunate enough to survive have moved away from the southern Sahara into","words":[["fortunate",334.24,334.66],["enough",334.66,335.04],["to",335.04,335.22],["survive",335.22,335.62],["have",335.62,336.18],["moved",336.18,336.4],["away",336.4,336.7],["from",336.7,336.92],["the",336.92,337.1],["southern",337.1,337.32],["Sahara",337.32,337.78],["into",337.78,338.18]]},{"start":338.18,"end":344.02,"text":"Burkina Faso in order to find new grazing lands for their herds. If there's","words":[["Burkina",338.18,338.98],["Faso",338.98,339.38],["in",339.38,339.78],["order",339.78,340.0],["to",340.0,340.16],["find",340.16,340.4],["new",340.4,340.64],["grazing",340.64,340.98],["lands",340.98,341.36],["for",341.36,341.78],["their",341.78,341.98],["herds.",341.98,342.38],["If",343.14,343.72],["there's",343.72,344.02]]},{"start":344.02,"end":348.64,"text":"One city which people associate with the Sahara Desert is probably Timbuktu.","words":[["One",344.02,344.1],["city",344.1,344.38],["which",344.38,344.6],["people",344.6,344.88],["associate",344.88,345.46],["with",345.46,345.72],["the",345.72,345.86],["Sahara",345.86,346.2],["Desert",346.2,346.52],["is",346.52,347.28],["probably",347.28,347.7],["Timbuktu.",347.7,348.64]]},{"start":349.64,"end":356.32,"text":"But what most people don't know is that Timbuktu was founded by Tuareg nomads almost a thousand","words":[["But",349.64,349.98],["what",349.98,350.12],["most",350.12,350.38],["people",350.38,350.64],["don't",350.64,351.04],["know",351.04,351.28],["is",351.28,351.8],["that",351.8,351.96],["Timbuktu",351.96,352.64],["was",352.64,353.32],["founded",353.32,353.64],["by",353.64,353.9],["Tuareg",353.9,354.42],["nomads",354.42,354.94],["almost",354.94,355.52],["a",355.52,355.98],["thousand",355.98,356.32]]},{"start":356.32,"end":357.18,"text":"years ago.","words":[["years",356.32,356.76],["ago.",356.76,357.18]]},{"start":358.28,"end":361.88,"text":"The city became the focal point of the Trans-Saharan caravan routes.","words":[["The",358.28,358.6],["city",358.6,358.8],["became",358.8,359.12],["the",359.12,359.32],["focal",359.32,359.6],["point",359.6,359.92],["of",359.92,360.1],["the",360.1,360.24],["Trans",360.24,360.52],["-Saharan",360.52,361.02],["caravan",361.02,361.54],["routes.",361.54,361.88]]},{"start":362.86,"end":368.68,"text":"North African merchants flocked there to do business and trading in gold and salt flourished.","words":[["North",362.86,363.42],["African",363.42,363.94],["merchants",363.94,364.54],["flocked",364.54,365.06],["there",365.06,365.24],["to",365.24,365.36],["do",365.36,365.5],["business",365.5,365.86],["and",365.86,366.64],["trading",366.64,366.94],["in",366.94,367.16],["gold",367.16,367.4],["and",367.4,367.68],["salt",367.68,368.02],["flourished.",368.02,368.68]]},{"start":368.68,"end":373.46,"text":"For many years, Timbuktu was considered inaccessible.","words":[["For",368.68,369.86],["many",369.86,370.12],["years,",370.12,370.56],["Timbuktu",371.0,371.54],["was",371.54,371.78],["considered",371.78,372.28],["inaccessible.",372.28,373.46]]},{"start":374.22,"end":378.08,"text":"But today, what is left of the city attracts a small number of tourists.","words":[["But",374.22,374.48],["today,",374.48,375.0],["what",375.28,375.44],["is",375.44,375.58],["left",375.58,375.84],["of",375.84,376.02],["the",376.02,376.12],["city",376.12,376.44],["attracts",376.44,376.98],["a",376.98,377.26],["small",377.26,377.42],["number",377.42,377.72],["of",377.72,377.88],["tourists.",377.88,378.08]]},{"start":379.36,"end":384.64,"text":"The tourism department of the Mali government employs some Tuaregs who act as guides.","words":[["The",379.36,379.58],["tourism",379.58,380.06],["department",380.06,380.56],["of",380.56,381.02],["the",381.02,381.18],["Mali",381.18,381.48],["government",381.48,381.88],["employs",381.88,382.54],["some",382.54,382.86],["Tuaregs",382.86,383.5],["who",383.5,383.86],["act",383.86,384.06],["as",384.06,384.24],["guides.",384.24,384.64]]},{"start":385.4,"end":393.02,"text":"Essential really, when you realize that it's only the Tuaregs who can find their way around the desert using the sand dunes as landmarks.","words":[["Essential",385.4,385.86],["really,",385.86,386.32],["when",386.52,386.62],["you",386.62,386.76],["realize",386.76,387.12],["that",387.12,387.34],["it's",387.34,387.52],["only",387.52,387.76],["the",387.76,387.94],["Tuaregs",387.94,388.58],["who",388.58,388.96],["can",388.96,389.1],["find",389.1,389.36],["their",389.36,389.58],["way",389.58,389.76],["around",389.76,390.14],["the",390.14,390.3],["desert",390.3,390.62],["using",390.62,391.22],["the",391.22,391.46],["sand",391.46,391.7],["dunes",391.7,392.1],["as",392.1,392.2],["landmarks.",392.2,393.02]]},{"start":394.38,"end":403.08,"text":"Right. I'll take questions now, before I go on to discuss Tamashek, the language spoken by the Tuaregs, which also has an alphabet called...","words":[["Right.",394.38,394.98],["I'll",395.46,395.6],["take",395.6,395.78],["questions",395.78,396.26],["now,",396.26,396.6],["before",397.0,397.2],["I",397.2,397.4],["go",397.4,397.54],["on",397.54,397.68],["to",397.68,397.78],["discuss",397.78,398.12],["Tamashek,",398.12,399.04],["the",399.48,399.6],["language",399.6,399.9],["spoken",399.9,400.28],["by",400.28,400.58],["the",400.58,400.8],["Tuaregs,",400.8,401.42],["which",401.72,401.9],["also",401.9,402.1],["has",402.1,402.36],["an",402.36,402.46],["alphabet",402.46,402.78],["called...",402.78,403.08]]}]}